1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:30,000
= kissasia.net =

2
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,002
(Scenes with child actors were filmed
safely with guardians and staff present.)

3
00:00:03,937 --> 00:00:06,171
The child I had waited so long for,

4
00:00:08,342 --> 00:00:11,311
the child I cherished
more than my own life,

5
00:00:14,161 --> 00:00:16,328
suddenly slipped away one day.

6
00:00:19,273 --> 00:00:20,673
I blamed the world,

7
00:00:21,389 --> 00:00:22,789
and I blamed myself.

8
00:00:24,658 --> 00:00:28,362
I hated myself
for failing to protect my baby...

9
00:00:30,230 --> 00:00:32,431
and I even tried to end my own life.

10
00:00:35,936 --> 00:00:36,834
And yet,

11
00:00:39,172 --> 00:00:40,339
to this very day,

12
00:00:43,210 --> 00:00:44,844
to protect my husband,

13
00:00:47,381 --> 00:00:50,316
I was ready to take that truth
to my grave.

14
00:00:53,854 --> 00:00:54,787
Today,

15
00:00:57,057 --> 00:00:58,492
I'm finally finding the courage...

16
00:01:01,629 --> 00:01:04,864
to speak the secret
I've buried in my heart...

17
00:01:06,567 --> 00:01:08,133
for the past three years.

18
00:01:11,772 --> 00:01:12,605
After...

19
00:01:17,177 --> 00:01:18,979
taking the pills my husband gave me,

20
00:01:20,314 --> 00:01:21,482
I lost my child.

21
00:01:24,852 --> 00:01:27,887
My husband gave me medication
I never should have taken.

22
00:01:29,590 --> 00:01:30,623
My husband...

23
00:01:32,359 --> 00:01:34,760
is the killer who caused our baby's death.

24
00:01:39,867 --> 00:01:40,834
Plaintiff.

25
00:01:43,337 --> 00:01:45,705
Is what you're saying true?

26
00:01:46,073 --> 00:01:47,740
Yes, it's the truth.

27
00:01:51,879 --> 00:01:53,580
I confirmed it with the doctor...

28
00:01:54,615 --> 00:01:57,283
who treated me when I had the miscarriage.

29
00:01:58,553 --> 00:02:00,821
It turned out the medication
my husband gave me...

30
00:02:01,555 --> 00:02:03,255
was fatal to the fetus.

31
00:02:03,256 --> 00:02:06,192
What the hell are you talking about?
What are you trying to pull?

32
00:02:06,427 --> 00:02:09,929
Defendant, please calm down
and take your seat.

33
00:02:16,603 --> 00:02:19,004
Investigator, what she just said...

34
00:02:19,005 --> 00:02:20,806
has absolutely no basis in reality.

35
00:02:20,807 --> 00:02:23,409
I never gave her anything like that.
And more importantly,

36
00:02:23,410 --> 00:02:24,710
why on earth...

37
00:02:25,078 --> 00:02:26,680
would I ever hurt my own child?

38
00:02:26,681 --> 00:02:28,514
This is absurd, Investigator.

39
00:02:28,515 --> 00:02:29,882
No, Investigator.

40
00:02:32,786 --> 00:02:33,753
Every word I said...

41
00:02:34,489 --> 00:02:36,455
- is the truth.
- Hey!

42
00:02:36,456 --> 00:02:37,990
Silence.

43
00:02:43,530 --> 00:02:46,932
I don't think we can continue
today's evaluation.

44
00:02:47,294 --> 00:02:49,395
We'll reschedule and continue next time.

45
00:02:52,272 --> 00:02:53,272
Have you lost your mind?

46
00:02:53,804 --> 00:02:55,265
You should've told them
what actually happened.

47
00:02:55,290 --> 00:02:57,309
Why make up such an insane lie?

48
00:02:57,310 --> 00:02:58,578
I'm not making anything up.

49
00:02:59,146 --> 00:03:01,748
Why would I go this far
just to invent a story?

50
00:03:01,948 --> 00:03:04,183
Then what medication
are you claiming I gave you?

51
00:03:04,451 --> 00:03:05,819
Do you really not remember?

52
00:03:06,087 --> 00:03:07,620
Whether it was medication
or anything else,

53
00:03:07,621 --> 00:03:10,456
I have never given you anything harmful.

54
00:03:10,792 --> 00:03:12,091
Then take this chance...

55
00:03:12,726 --> 00:03:14,261
to think long and hard about it.

56
00:03:15,162 --> 00:03:18,030
Think about whether everything you gave me
was actually good for me,

57
00:03:18,031 --> 00:03:19,166
medication or otherwise.

58
00:03:19,466 --> 00:03:20,533
Unbelievable.

59
00:03:23,336 --> 00:03:24,236
Fine.

60
00:03:24,545 --> 00:03:27,279
Let's say, for a second, you actually had
this ridiculous misunderstanding.

61
00:03:27,808 --> 00:03:29,408
Then why didn't you ever say
a word until now?

62
00:03:29,977 --> 00:03:31,411
Why stay quiet all this time...

63
00:03:31,412 --> 00:03:33,279
only to cause a scene here?

64
00:03:34,581 --> 00:03:35,749
I wanted to...

65
00:03:37,517 --> 00:03:39,184
carry it alone if I could.

66
00:03:41,055 --> 00:03:42,789
I was afraid it would tear you apart.

67
00:03:43,757 --> 00:03:45,357
- But...
- But what?

68
00:03:48,128 --> 00:03:49,095
But what?

69
00:03:49,430 --> 00:03:50,929
I just don't want to anymore.

70
00:03:52,966 --> 00:03:56,235
I can't wait to see
how you treat me from now on.

71
00:03:57,138 --> 00:03:58,714
You were so worried sick about Hee Ju...

72
00:03:58,739 --> 00:04:01,874
just because she took a few pills.

73
00:04:08,582 --> 00:04:09,615
Geez.

74
00:04:12,152 --> 00:04:13,487
Do you honestly not remember?

75
00:04:20,193 --> 00:04:22,295
If what your wife said is true,

76
00:04:22,863 --> 00:04:24,564
this is extremely serious.

77
00:04:25,232 --> 00:04:26,966
She claims she even got
a medical opinion...

78
00:04:26,967 --> 00:04:28,667
from the doctor who treated her.

79
00:04:29,269 --> 00:04:32,171
But I don't even remember
buying any medication myself.

80
00:04:32,172 --> 00:04:35,007
Then you should've pressed her
for details.

81
00:04:35,008 --> 00:04:37,343
This isn't something
you can just brush off.

82
00:04:37,544 --> 00:04:40,446
Apart from the divorce,

83
00:04:40,781 --> 00:04:42,414
this could easily amount
to attempted murder.

84
00:04:42,849 --> 00:04:44,049
Attempted murder?

85
00:04:44,751 --> 00:04:46,486
Then could that mean...

86
00:04:46,487 --> 00:04:49,088
the reason my wife stabbed me
back then was...

87
00:04:49,089 --> 00:04:50,956
That's entirely possible.

88
00:04:50,957 --> 00:04:53,993
If she believed her baby died
because of pills her husband gave her,

89
00:04:53,994 --> 00:04:57,496
she would've been in a completely
fragile and volatile state.

90
00:04:57,497 --> 00:05:00,365
I'm the one who's completely rattled here.

91
00:05:00,734 --> 00:05:03,469
I never know when or where
she's going to drop another bomb,

92
00:05:03,704 --> 00:05:05,972
so I'm constantly on edge.
It's driving me crazy.

93
00:05:06,707 --> 00:05:08,935
Is that why you were so terrified
of getting caught cheating...

94
00:05:08,960 --> 00:05:11,144
that you actually made her sign
a written contract?

95
00:05:11,611 --> 00:05:14,046
What does that have to do with anything?

96
00:05:14,716 --> 00:05:16,816
Look, just get to the bottom of this.

97
00:05:16,817 --> 00:05:18,418
If there's been a misunderstanding,
clear it up.

98
00:05:19,152 --> 00:05:20,152
All right.

99
00:05:21,855 --> 00:05:23,255
And cut things off
with your girlfriend too.

100
00:05:24,225 --> 00:05:25,057
What?

101
00:05:26,059 --> 00:05:28,627
What, you're going to keep
seeing her on the side?

102
00:05:28,762 --> 00:05:31,116
That affair is what triggered
this entire disaster in the first place.

103
00:05:32,333 --> 00:05:33,399
Seriously.

104
00:05:45,779 --> 00:05:47,113
Good morning.

105
00:05:48,415 --> 00:05:49,782
What's with the faces?

106
00:05:49,783 --> 00:05:51,617
You look like you've seen a ghost.

107
00:05:51,884 --> 00:05:53,986
Don't you have a job?

108
00:05:54,154 --> 00:05:56,255
You seem awfully free
for a weekday morning.

109
00:05:57,791 --> 00:05:59,425
I'm a freelancer.

110
00:05:59,861 --> 00:06:01,294
I take the day off when there's no work.

111
00:06:01,696 --> 00:06:04,230
And today just happens to be
one of those days.

112
00:06:06,500 --> 00:06:08,433
Right. Let me see your phone for a second.

113
00:06:08,804 --> 00:06:10,803
- What?
- Just give it here.

114
00:06:13,507 --> 00:06:16,642
My name is An Hee Ju.

115
00:06:17,177 --> 00:06:18,310
Not "ma'am."

116
00:06:19,847 --> 00:06:22,414
Save my number, just in case.

117
00:06:22,415 --> 00:06:24,459
That way, you won't have
to break down my door again.

118
00:06:24,484 --> 00:06:26,785
Oh, so your last name is An. An Hee Ju.

119
00:06:26,786 --> 00:06:29,421
Why are you even saving that?

120
00:06:31,091 --> 00:06:32,558
I'll keep this brief.

121
00:06:32,693 --> 00:06:34,393
Move out today.

122
00:06:34,394 --> 00:06:36,963
I'll give you a full refund for the month.

123
00:06:36,964 --> 00:06:39,164
Mom, that's throwing money away.

124
00:06:39,165 --> 00:06:41,801
I'd rather lose money than let this girl
stress me into an early grave.

125
00:06:42,336 --> 00:06:43,969
You're moving out today, right?

126
00:06:44,437 --> 00:06:46,071
- No, I'm not.
- What?

127
00:06:47,140 --> 00:06:48,574
Mother,

128
00:06:48,708 --> 00:06:50,842
please don't hate me so much.

129
00:06:51,278 --> 00:06:53,580
You're Mr. Ji's mother, after all,

130
00:06:53,581 --> 00:06:55,149
so I'd like for us to get along.

131
00:06:55,150 --> 00:06:56,249
What?

132
00:06:56,917 --> 00:06:59,318
How dare you call me Mother!

133
00:06:59,319 --> 00:07:01,453
Oh, you don't like that?

134
00:07:01,855 --> 00:07:04,423
Then I'll just call you Grandma.

135
00:07:04,591 --> 00:07:06,158
Honestly, that rolls off the tongue
better anyway.

136
00:07:06,993 --> 00:07:07,960
Grandma,

137
00:07:09,430 --> 00:07:10,930
I'm heading upstairs now.

138
00:07:15,735 --> 00:07:16,835
Grandma?

139
00:07:19,073 --> 00:07:20,139
Mom, you are a grandma.

140
00:07:20,608 --> 00:07:21,507
Why, you little...

141
00:07:41,228 --> 00:07:45,631
Two lines means pregnant, right?

142
00:07:46,032 --> 00:07:48,301
Honey, are you pregnant?
Are you really pregnant?

143
00:07:50,438 --> 00:07:53,807
I'm going to be a dad! You did it!

144
00:07:53,808 --> 00:07:55,874
The child I had waited so long for,

145
00:07:57,844 --> 00:08:00,879
the child I cherished
more than my own life,

146
00:08:03,650 --> 00:08:05,851
suddenly slipped away one day.

147
00:08:10,190 --> 00:08:11,123
After...

148
00:08:12,993 --> 00:08:14,593
taking the pills my husband gave me,

149
00:08:16,129 --> 00:08:17,297
I lost my child.

150
00:08:19,099 --> 00:08:21,033
My husband gave me medication...

151
00:08:21,502 --> 00:08:22,768
I never should have taken.

152
00:08:24,704 --> 00:08:25,704
My husband...

153
00:08:27,007 --> 00:08:29,508
is the killer who caused our baby's death.

154
00:08:42,756 --> 00:08:44,924
Are you sure
you didn't misunderstand something?

155
00:08:45,058 --> 00:08:47,326
I already had all the ingredients
tested and analyzed.

156
00:08:47,829 --> 00:08:49,729
That medication was the direct cause...

157
00:08:50,229 --> 00:08:51,296
of my miscarriage.

158
00:08:55,102 --> 00:08:57,702
How could medication cause
a miscarriage, though?

159
00:08:58,038 --> 00:09:01,541
It must have been made
to support your health in the first place.

160
00:09:01,542 --> 00:09:04,410
That's right.
It was made to improve health.

161
00:09:05,212 --> 00:09:06,045
The problem was...

162
00:09:07,181 --> 00:09:09,982
it was something pregnant women
should never take.

163
00:09:14,455 --> 00:09:15,654
Do you remember...

164
00:09:16,656 --> 00:09:19,358
when you started taking it?

165
00:09:20,160 --> 00:09:21,260
Let me see.

166
00:09:21,728 --> 00:09:24,163
Ji Won Ho gave it to me...

167
00:09:24,665 --> 00:09:26,533
around Chuseok,

168
00:09:27,601 --> 00:09:29,702
so I must have taken it
for at least two months.

169
00:09:30,603 --> 00:09:31,670
Around Chuseok?

170
00:09:32,071 --> 00:09:33,805
We were swamped back then...

171
00:09:33,806 --> 00:09:35,741
because of a group wedding we sponsored.

172
00:09:36,176 --> 00:09:38,144
I was so busy I'd skip meals,

173
00:09:38,145 --> 00:09:40,312
but I never once missed
taking those pills.

174
00:09:42,782 --> 00:09:44,149
Taking that medication...

175
00:09:45,986 --> 00:09:49,421
is the single biggest regret of my life.

176
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:02,434
What's wrong? Why do you look like that?

177
00:10:05,305 --> 00:10:06,272
It's nothing.

178
00:10:10,410 --> 00:10:12,678
Anyway, that must have been
devastating for you.

179
00:10:14,048 --> 00:10:14,914
To be honest,

180
00:10:15,748 --> 00:10:17,014
it still hurts.

181
00:10:19,219 --> 00:10:20,652
Even after all this time,

182
00:10:21,388 --> 00:10:22,988
I haven't really moved past it.

183
00:10:30,630 --> 00:10:32,998
The lawyer is here.
I'll head upstairs first.

184
00:10:33,667 --> 00:10:34,801
I hope the meeting goes well.

185
00:10:34,868 --> 00:10:36,502
- Could you clear this away for me?
- Sure.

186
00:10:36,503 --> 00:10:37,637
- I'm sorry about this.
- Don't be.

187
00:10:42,142 --> 00:10:43,709
That really happened to you?

188
00:10:44,544 --> 00:10:45,612
But why...

189
00:10:46,814 --> 00:10:48,914
Why didn't you tell me sooner?

190
00:10:49,450 --> 00:10:51,884
- What?
- If something that serious happened,

191
00:10:52,052 --> 00:10:54,686
we wouldn't have had to take
such a roundabout route.

192
00:10:56,623 --> 00:10:58,557
Are you certain
it was your husband's mistake?

193
00:10:58,792 --> 00:11:00,759
If there were any sign
he did it on purpose...

194
00:11:00,760 --> 00:11:02,394
Absolutely not.

195
00:11:03,496 --> 00:11:04,629
My husband...

196
00:11:05,333 --> 00:11:08,300
wanted a child just as badly as I did.

197
00:11:09,535 --> 00:11:12,003
He had no reason to do
something like that deliberately.

198
00:11:13,006 --> 00:11:14,840
If that's the case,

199
00:11:15,876 --> 00:11:17,243
doesn't that make it even stranger?

200
00:11:19,078 --> 00:11:23,548
If your husband bought medicine
specifically to support your health,

201
00:11:24,217 --> 00:11:26,753
he surely would've asked
the most basic questions at the pharmacy.

202
00:11:27,354 --> 00:11:28,253
You're right.

203
00:11:28,765 --> 00:11:30,231
Even as he bought it...

204
00:11:30,256 --> 00:11:33,391
He should've made sure
it was safe for a pregnant woman.

205
00:11:34,395 --> 00:11:36,028
Yet the medicine you took...

206
00:11:36,496 --> 00:11:39,398
turned out to be hazardous
for pregnant women.

207
00:11:40,166 --> 00:11:43,568
I just assumed my husband had been
reckless and careless.

208
00:11:43,904 --> 00:11:45,838
Could there have been a mix-up...

209
00:11:46,806 --> 00:11:48,774
somewhere along the line?

210
00:11:49,175 --> 00:11:50,475
A mix-up?

211
00:11:56,717 --> 00:11:59,485
There's no way you would've given
Mi Young medicine like that.

212
00:12:00,554 --> 00:12:03,188
Isn't she going too far
just to get the upper hand in the divorce?

213
00:12:03,389 --> 00:12:07,192
Mi Young isn't the type
to fabricate something like that.

214
00:12:10,797 --> 00:12:11,764
Wait a second.

215
00:12:12,199 --> 00:12:14,099
Did you just think of something?

216
00:12:16,636 --> 00:12:17,870
Could it be that?

217
00:12:20,039 --> 00:12:22,941
It'd be such a waste to return this.

218
00:12:25,011 --> 00:12:26,812
If you bought this out of pocket,

219
00:12:26,947 --> 00:12:29,215
it'd easily run you hundreds of dollars.

220
00:12:31,050 --> 00:12:32,917
What could possibly cost that much?

221
00:12:33,453 --> 00:12:35,087
Look,

222
00:12:35,691 --> 00:12:38,958
it's a Chuseok gift
delivered to the company.

223
00:12:39,559 --> 00:12:42,627
Ms. Baek specifically said
to immediately return...

224
00:12:42,628 --> 00:12:44,930
any gifts that could look like bribes.

225
00:12:45,464 --> 00:12:46,865
Then just send it back.

226
00:12:46,866 --> 00:12:48,834
We'll only get in trouble if we keep it.

227
00:12:49,003 --> 00:12:51,904
It's just not entirely clear...

228
00:12:51,905 --> 00:12:54,173
if this was meant as a favor or not.

229
00:12:54,474 --> 00:12:55,641
Who sent it?

230
00:12:58,078 --> 00:13:00,712
A massive conglomerate.

231
00:13:01,082 --> 00:13:02,915
The kind of company
that wouldn't think twice...

232
00:13:02,916 --> 00:13:05,351
about handing out something this pricey.

233
00:13:06,286 --> 00:13:07,219
Really?

234
00:13:07,754 --> 00:13:08,687
Mr. Ji,

235
00:13:09,021 --> 00:13:12,624
this tonic is supposed to be
top-of-the-line.

236
00:13:13,158 --> 00:13:15,527
Word is, taking even one pill
gives you an incredible boost.

237
00:13:16,196 --> 00:13:17,296
An incredible boost?

238
00:13:17,597 --> 00:13:18,497
Yes.

239
00:13:21,134 --> 00:13:22,401
Why don't we give it...

240
00:13:23,003 --> 00:13:24,302
to Mi Young?

241
00:13:25,038 --> 00:13:25,938
Mi Young?

242
00:13:26,073 --> 00:13:29,542
She's barely eating these days
because of her morning sickness.

243
00:13:29,543 --> 00:13:31,643
Something like this might
actually do her some good.

244
00:13:32,980 --> 00:13:35,447
Mi Young will hit the roof
if she finds out.

245
00:13:36,583 --> 00:13:38,116
So,

246
00:13:38,519 --> 00:13:40,886
just don't tell her
it came from a corporate partner.

247
00:13:41,354 --> 00:13:43,689
Tell her you bought it for her yourself.

248
00:13:44,491 --> 00:13:45,390
How does that sound?

249
00:13:45,391 --> 00:13:47,259
You gave that to Mi Young?

250
00:13:47,860 --> 00:13:48,726
Yeah.

251
00:13:49,361 --> 00:13:51,229
I gave it to her and claimed
I bought it myself.

252
00:13:51,298 --> 00:13:53,398
Did you even check what was in it first?

253
00:13:54,434 --> 00:13:56,204
Ms. Song said
it was high-end and effective,

254
00:13:56,228 --> 00:13:57,336
so I just took her word for it.

255
00:13:57,337 --> 00:13:58,703
Still, she was pregnant.

256
00:13:58,704 --> 00:14:01,072
You should've checked
the ingredients thoroughly.

257
00:14:01,608 --> 00:14:04,310
Or you should've just been honest
and told her it was a gift from a client.

258
00:14:04,811 --> 00:14:06,712
Why pretend you bought it
out of your own pocket?

259
00:14:06,746 --> 00:14:09,448
You know how it is.
When women are pregnant,

260
00:14:09,449 --> 00:14:12,518
they want their husbands to fuss over them
and take care of them.

261
00:14:12,786 --> 00:14:15,654
I figured she'd feel loved
if I said I bought it myself.

262
00:14:15,955 --> 00:14:17,389
You were trying to look good
using a free gift,

263
00:14:17,657 --> 00:14:18,924
and look where that got you.

264
00:14:19,160 --> 00:14:21,627
Still, I doubt that medicine
had anything to do with it.

265
00:14:23,730 --> 00:14:26,264
I can't just sit here guessing.
I need to talk to Ms. Song directly.

266
00:14:26,265 --> 00:14:27,198
Wait a minute.

267
00:14:30,136 --> 00:14:32,304
What if it really was the medicine
Ms. Song handed you?

268
00:14:32,871 --> 00:14:33,838
What then?

269
00:14:34,508 --> 00:14:35,440
What do you mean?

270
00:14:35,441 --> 00:14:38,311
If Ms. Song finds out her best friend
miscarried because of her,

271
00:14:39,479 --> 00:14:40,379
how do you think...

272
00:14:41,249 --> 00:14:42,382
she's going to take that?

273
00:14:43,550 --> 00:14:45,417
It would crush her.

274
00:14:46,286 --> 00:14:48,420
I know it's not my place to step in,

275
00:14:49,657 --> 00:14:51,390
but you need to think this through.

276
00:14:52,125 --> 00:14:53,992
You two keep raking up the past...

277
00:14:54,127 --> 00:14:56,061
and hurting each other over it.

278
00:14:57,330 --> 00:14:59,231
What happened to the baby
is heartbreaking,

279
00:14:59,532 --> 00:15:01,599
but losing Ms. Song in the crossfire...

280
00:15:02,135 --> 00:15:03,334
would be another tragedy.

281
00:15:04,338 --> 00:15:05,939
I still need to know the truth.

282
00:15:05,940 --> 00:15:08,273
For all we know, she might not have
anything to do with it.

283
00:15:08,274 --> 00:15:09,363
From everything we've put together,

284
00:15:09,387 --> 00:15:11,076
it looks like Ms. Song made
an honest mistake.

285
00:15:11,077 --> 00:15:13,445
All right, I hear you.

286
00:15:14,181 --> 00:15:16,181
I'll bring it up when the timing is right.

287
00:15:16,283 --> 00:15:17,784
I'll make sure it doesn't blindside her.

288
00:15:24,724 --> 00:15:26,858
(Nutrition Facts, Health Benefits,
and Directions)

289
00:15:31,497 --> 00:15:32,831
(Supplements pregnant women
shouldn't take)

290
00:15:36,769 --> 00:15:37,802
Ms. Song.

291
00:15:39,038 --> 00:15:40,438
Yes, Mr. Kang.

292
00:15:40,873 --> 00:15:41,706
Are you all right?

293
00:15:42,175 --> 00:15:44,877
Why? What do you mean?

294
00:15:45,511 --> 00:15:47,045
Oh, nothing.

295
00:15:48,214 --> 00:15:50,515
By the way,
did you submit that fabric order?

296
00:15:51,184 --> 00:15:52,450
Oh, that's right.

297
00:15:52,752 --> 00:15:54,786
I was supposed
to put that order through today.

298
00:15:55,355 --> 00:15:57,822
I'm sorry. It completely slipped my mind.

299
00:15:58,959 --> 00:16:00,525
Please handle that right away
this morning.

300
00:16:01,161 --> 00:16:03,128
Understood. I'll process it right now.

301
00:16:21,547 --> 00:16:23,782
(Jihwaja Motel)

302
00:16:26,586 --> 00:16:28,654
We can't just kick the girl out
on the street.

303
00:16:29,122 --> 00:16:30,289
So what are we supposed to do?

304
00:16:30,523 --> 00:16:32,891
Should we just act
like nothing happened for now?

305
00:16:32,959 --> 00:16:35,260
And let her cause another scene?

306
00:16:35,828 --> 00:16:36,761
Fair point.

307
00:16:37,397 --> 00:16:39,098
Just having her here puts me on edge.

308
00:16:40,166 --> 00:16:43,401
Mom, what if we pipe some smoke
under her door?

309
00:16:43,569 --> 00:16:45,637
- What?
- If she smells smoke,

310
00:16:45,638 --> 00:16:46,905
she'll panic and run out on her own.

311
00:16:46,973 --> 00:16:49,708
Are you going to burn
the whole building down over one nuisance?

312
00:16:51,677 --> 00:16:54,178
The girl seems normal enough
on the surface.

313
00:16:54,179 --> 00:16:55,680
What does she even see in Won Ho anyway?

314
00:16:55,681 --> 00:16:57,215
What's not to like?

315
00:16:57,216 --> 00:16:59,684
Our Won Ho is handsome,
capable, and sharp.

316
00:16:59,685 --> 00:17:01,252
He can hold his own anywhere.

317
00:17:01,521 --> 00:17:02,955
Even if he shakes off that little vixen,

318
00:17:02,956 --> 00:17:04,923
he could easily remarry two more times!

319
00:17:05,124 --> 00:17:07,193
Remarrying twice might be pushing it, Mom.

320
00:17:09,095 --> 00:17:09,928
Mom,

321
00:17:10,430 --> 00:17:12,164
- that's it.
- What?

322
00:17:12,999 --> 00:17:14,866
You're not the first, you know.

323
00:17:15,268 --> 00:17:17,670
Before you, there was the girl
in Room 203.

324
00:17:17,671 --> 00:17:19,437
And before her, the one in Room 403.

325
00:17:19,705 --> 00:17:22,540
A whole parade of women after Won Ho
have come and gone.

326
00:17:22,842 --> 00:17:25,844
To him, you're just another passing fling.

327
00:17:26,412 --> 00:17:28,279
The only woman who will stand
by Won Ho's side to the very end...

328
00:17:28,514 --> 00:17:29,714
is Mi Young.

329
00:17:35,087 --> 00:17:36,387
Was something I said funny to you?

330
00:17:38,324 --> 00:17:40,892
No. Just pathetic.

331
00:17:41,694 --> 00:17:43,628
- What?
- It's pathetic.

332
00:17:44,063 --> 00:17:45,797
Watching you scramble to invent stories...

333
00:17:45,965 --> 00:17:47,465
just to scare me into leaving.

334
00:17:47,466 --> 00:17:49,367
I'm telling you the cold, hard truth.

335
00:17:49,602 --> 00:17:51,136
Save your breath.

336
00:17:51,536 --> 00:17:53,615
I don't care how many women
have drifted in and out of his life.

337
00:17:53,640 --> 00:17:55,273
I'm not going anywhere.

338
00:17:55,541 --> 00:17:57,443
What could you possibly see in Won Ho?

339
00:17:57,944 --> 00:17:58,810
It's simple.

340
00:17:59,745 --> 00:18:00,812
He's my destiny.

341
00:18:00,813 --> 00:18:01,646
What on earth?

342
00:18:01,671 --> 00:18:03,139
I knew it the second I laid eyes on him.

343
00:18:03,216 --> 00:18:06,585
I knew Mr. Ji was the man
I was destined to be with.

344
00:18:06,787 --> 00:18:09,321
All right, that's enough out of you.
If you keep pushing this...

345
00:18:09,322 --> 00:18:11,657
You're the one who needs to back off.

346
00:18:12,157 --> 00:18:13,357
When I lose my temper,

347
00:18:14,461 --> 00:18:15,761
I can get really nasty.

348
00:18:16,229 --> 00:18:18,230
And what are you going to do, get violent?

349
00:18:18,832 --> 00:18:20,565
Are you going to lay a hand on me?

350
00:18:21,467 --> 00:18:22,967
Oh, that's right.

351
00:18:24,104 --> 00:18:26,571
I should take care of that first.

352
00:18:31,110 --> 00:18:34,879
Hello. Is this customer support
for the pharmaceutical division?

353
00:18:35,715 --> 00:18:39,084
I'd like to check some information
on one of your products.

354
00:18:39,652 --> 00:18:40,485
Yes.

355
00:18:41,053 --> 00:18:44,189
The specific product
I'm calling about is...

356
00:18:44,890 --> 00:18:46,157
Ms. Song.

357
00:18:46,960 --> 00:18:49,094
I'll have to call back in a moment.

358
00:18:50,363 --> 00:18:52,997
What's going on?

359
00:18:52,998 --> 00:18:56,702
Ms. Song, you need to get
to the main office right now.

360
00:18:57,604 --> 00:18:59,270
How could you make
such a careless mistake?

361
00:18:59,639 --> 00:19:02,407
How do you accidentally add an extra zero?

362
00:19:02,741 --> 00:19:04,543
Thank goodness I caught it
before the purchase went through!

363
00:19:04,743 --> 00:19:07,311
Do you have any idea
what kind of mess that would've made?

364
00:19:08,048 --> 00:19:10,381
I'm so sorry. Truly, I am.

365
00:19:10,718 --> 00:19:11,584
Ms. Song.

366
00:19:12,084 --> 00:19:14,152
Where on earth has your head been today?

367
00:19:16,956 --> 00:19:17,856
Mr. Kang,

368
00:19:18,724 --> 00:19:20,358
I think that's enough.

369
00:19:21,226 --> 00:19:23,561
We caught it in time,
so no real harm done.

370
00:19:29,735 --> 00:19:30,768
From the look on her face,

371
00:19:31,771 --> 00:19:33,105
I think Ms. Song already realized...

372
00:19:33,339 --> 00:19:34,939
what mistake she made.

373
00:19:35,241 --> 00:19:36,107
What?

374
00:19:36,375 --> 00:19:38,076
Already? How could she know?

375
00:19:38,077 --> 00:19:39,845
Mi Young must have brought it up to her.

376
00:19:40,279 --> 00:19:42,747
I happened to glance
at her screen earlier,

377
00:19:44,116 --> 00:19:46,317
and she was looking up herbal tonics.

378
00:19:48,287 --> 00:19:50,888
"Supplements pregnant women
shouldn't take."

379
00:20:12,812 --> 00:20:14,680
Yes? What is it?

380
00:20:15,881 --> 00:20:18,416
That place? I like it too.

381
00:20:19,785 --> 00:20:20,685
Great.

382
00:20:21,454 --> 00:20:22,353
What time?

383
00:20:24,590 --> 00:20:26,157
Okay, sounds good.

384
00:20:26,893 --> 00:20:29,060
Should I just say
the reservation is under Calvin?

385
00:20:30,563 --> 00:20:31,997
All right, see you then.

386
00:20:35,067 --> 00:20:36,467
You scared me.

387
00:20:37,203 --> 00:20:39,038
Why are you sneaking up on me?

388
00:20:39,039 --> 00:20:40,540
Why so startled?

389
00:20:40,541 --> 00:20:42,474
Do I need to kick the door open?

390
00:20:42,808 --> 00:20:44,609
Do you have something to say?

391
00:20:44,911 --> 00:20:47,045
You seem pretty close with Calvin lately.

392
00:20:47,613 --> 00:20:50,481
- What?
- Going somewhere nice together again?

393
00:20:50,716 --> 00:20:52,083
What's it to you?

394
00:20:52,484 --> 00:20:55,120
You're like the couple of the century
who will never break up.

395
00:20:56,055 --> 00:20:57,121
"The couple of the century?"

396
00:20:57,622 --> 00:21:00,124
I have work to do.
Say what you have to say and get out.

397
00:21:03,295 --> 00:21:04,629
If it really was...

398
00:21:06,133 --> 00:21:08,099
that medicine that caused the problem,

399
00:21:10,236 --> 00:21:12,003
could you forgive the person
who gave it to you?

400
00:21:13,139 --> 00:21:14,038
What?

401
00:21:14,039 --> 00:21:17,042
If it wasn't me, but someone else,

402
00:21:18,344 --> 00:21:19,911
could you forgive that person?

403
00:21:21,781 --> 00:21:22,681
Either way,

404
00:21:24,583 --> 00:21:25,783
the fact remains,

405
00:21:26,986 --> 00:21:28,320
that I lost my baby,

406
00:21:29,522 --> 00:21:30,889
after taking that medicine.

407
00:21:32,291 --> 00:21:33,124
And,

408
00:21:34,427 --> 00:21:36,027
if it wasn't you,

409
00:21:36,429 --> 00:21:38,329
could I forgive that person?

410
00:21:40,733 --> 00:21:41,566
No.

411
00:21:43,703 --> 00:21:45,670
The only reason I put up with it
was that it was you.

412
00:21:47,807 --> 00:21:50,608
The only reason I was
able to endure three years of this was...

413
00:21:53,646 --> 00:21:56,715
because the person
who gave me that medicine was you,

414
00:21:58,884 --> 00:22:00,618
and no one else.

415
00:22:23,075 --> 00:22:23,975
I...

416
00:22:26,212 --> 00:22:27,812
lost my baby after taking medicine...

417
00:22:29,348 --> 00:22:30,481
my husband gave me.

418
00:22:40,125 --> 00:22:40,958
(Ms. Song)

419
00:22:40,959 --> 00:22:44,128
Mr. Ji. There's something important
I need to tell you.

420
00:22:44,597 --> 00:22:46,598
I'll be waiting at the cafe up ahead.

421
00:22:53,272 --> 00:22:54,272
Mr. Ji.

422
00:22:56,142 --> 00:22:59,744
The reason I asked you to meet me
outside like this is that...

423
00:23:00,479 --> 00:23:02,213
Because...

424
00:23:04,250 --> 00:23:06,184
You heard it from Mi Young, didn't you?

425
00:23:09,288 --> 00:23:10,188
About the medicine.

426
00:23:11,223 --> 00:23:12,123
Yes.

427
00:23:12,892 --> 00:23:13,959
She told me.

428
00:23:19,932 --> 00:23:20,999
Still, thank you.

429
00:23:21,501 --> 00:23:24,636
I wasn't sure
how to bring it up either, so...

430
00:23:26,038 --> 00:23:27,638
thanks for having the courage.

431
00:23:27,973 --> 00:23:29,407
But I really thought...

432
00:23:30,208 --> 00:23:32,243
there was no way anything could go wrong.

433
00:23:34,613 --> 00:23:35,546
I know.

434
00:23:38,784 --> 00:23:40,184
You're not a pharmacist.

435
00:23:40,185 --> 00:23:42,387
How could you possibly
know every ingredient?

436
00:23:43,622 --> 00:23:44,522
It was...

437
00:23:45,825 --> 00:23:47,325
just really bad luck.

438
00:23:48,326 --> 00:23:51,829
It just happened to be extremely
harmful for pregnant women.

439
00:23:53,399 --> 00:23:54,866
That's not it.

440
00:23:56,769 --> 00:23:57,736
What do you mean?

441
00:23:58,203 --> 00:24:02,574
That medicine was nothing more
than an ordinary health supplement.

442
00:24:02,575 --> 00:24:04,776
It was packed with ingredients
that are good for health.

443
00:24:05,444 --> 00:24:08,246
I called the pharmaceutical company
earlier and confirmed everything.

444
00:24:08,714 --> 00:24:09,747
Really?

445
00:24:11,383 --> 00:24:14,285
Yes, I knew it.

446
00:24:14,754 --> 00:24:16,488
It just didn't make sense.

447
00:24:18,758 --> 00:24:21,459
Ah Ri, I'm sorry. I misunderstood.

448
00:24:21,460 --> 00:24:22,860
I'm really sorry. Actually,

449
00:24:23,729 --> 00:24:24,729
thank you.

450
00:24:26,732 --> 00:24:28,232
No.

451
00:24:29,602 --> 00:24:30,868
It's my fault.

452
00:24:32,771 --> 00:24:34,038
Why is it your fault?

453
00:24:34,039 --> 00:24:36,073
You said nothing was
wrong with the medicine.

454
00:24:36,074 --> 00:24:38,676
Nothing was wrong with the medicine,

455
00:24:39,879 --> 00:24:41,947
but the person who gave it to me was...

456
00:24:44,917 --> 00:24:46,484
Calvin.

457
00:24:48,020 --> 00:24:48,953
What?

458
00:24:49,421 --> 00:24:50,421
Yes.

459
00:24:51,858 --> 00:24:53,391
The person who sent that medicine...

460
00:24:54,193 --> 00:24:55,860
was Calvin.

461
00:25:08,140 --> 00:25:09,640
I checked the package,

462
00:25:10,108 --> 00:25:12,443
and it was from Calvin.

463
00:25:13,178 --> 00:25:15,446
I knew Mi Young would
get angry if she found out,

464
00:25:15,949 --> 00:25:18,183
but it was something Calvin had sent,

465
00:25:18,451 --> 00:25:20,952
I thought it had to be good medicine.

466
00:25:20,953 --> 00:25:22,020
That's why I...

467
00:25:23,555 --> 00:25:24,522
If...

468
00:25:25,925 --> 00:25:26,958
Calvin did...

469
00:25:28,428 --> 00:25:31,329
something to that medicine...

470
00:25:35,301 --> 00:25:36,268
Three years ago,

471
00:25:37,403 --> 00:25:40,938
on the day the test confirmed
the child wasn't biologically mine,

472
00:25:41,774 --> 00:25:44,041
I happened to see
Mi Young at the hospital.

473
00:25:45,678 --> 00:25:47,712
She looked like she was pregnant.

474
00:25:51,417 --> 00:25:53,017
I couldn't bring myself to say hello,

475
00:25:53,852 --> 00:25:55,452
so I just watched her from a distance.

476
00:25:56,990 --> 00:25:58,423
Seeing Mi Young pregnant...

477
00:25:59,658 --> 00:26:00,891
I had mixed feelings.

478
00:26:03,829 --> 00:26:05,095
It was really bitter.

479
00:26:20,913 --> 00:26:24,315
Weren't we supposed to be
out of each other's lives?

480
00:26:24,717 --> 00:26:26,584
Maybe we could have been.

481
00:26:27,153 --> 00:26:29,086
If you hadn't done what you did to me.

482
00:26:29,922 --> 00:26:30,822
What did I do?

483
00:26:31,057 --> 00:26:32,523
You ordered someone to do it, right?

484
00:26:33,125 --> 00:26:34,492
To push me off that cliff.

485
00:26:34,827 --> 00:26:37,795
Are you still angry
about someone pushing you off a cliff?

486
00:26:38,530 --> 00:26:39,530
What did you just say?

487
00:26:39,732 --> 00:26:43,334
If you fell off a cliff
and still came out of it this unharmed,

488
00:26:44,236 --> 00:26:45,970
I'd be grateful if I were you.

489
00:26:48,374 --> 00:26:50,742
I'd feel like I'd been given a new life,

490
00:26:51,176 --> 00:26:52,444
and I'd want to live it,

491
00:26:53,112 --> 00:26:55,246
better than I did before.

492
00:26:57,316 --> 00:26:58,683
Are you kidding me right now?

493
00:27:00,385 --> 00:27:01,919
I'm going to get my revenge.

494
00:27:03,022 --> 00:27:04,738
I'll pay you back...

495
00:27:05,146 --> 00:27:06,791
exactly for what you did to me.

496
00:27:10,929 --> 00:27:11,761
Great.

497
00:27:12,265 --> 00:27:13,431
Try me anytime.

498
00:27:14,433 --> 00:27:15,500
But before you do,

499
00:27:16,169 --> 00:27:17,267
bring me some evidence.

500
00:27:18,037 --> 00:27:18,903
What?

501
00:27:18,904 --> 00:27:21,406
Evidence that I pushed you off that cliff.

502
00:27:22,674 --> 00:27:23,841
Before revenge or anything,

503
00:27:24,510 --> 00:27:26,744
isn't fact-checking the bare minimum?

504
00:27:35,254 --> 00:27:36,253
Yes.

505
00:27:36,254 --> 00:27:38,056
Mr. Kim, a guest has arrived.

506
00:27:38,390 --> 00:27:40,458
- Where's Calvin?
- Don't go yet.

507
00:27:40,459 --> 00:27:41,926
Is he here?

508
00:27:41,927 --> 00:27:43,227
Hold on.

509
00:27:44,096 --> 00:27:45,163
Mr. Ji.

510
00:27:46,398 --> 00:27:47,965
What brings you here at this hour?

511
00:27:48,099 --> 00:27:50,301
Something came to mind
that I wanted to ask you.

512
00:27:50,670 --> 00:27:52,536
You came here to confront him too?

513
00:27:52,537 --> 00:27:53,704
You stay out of this.

514
00:27:56,875 --> 00:27:58,208
I said, get out.

515
00:27:59,411 --> 00:28:00,244
Okay.

516
00:28:12,357 --> 00:28:13,524
What is it you want to know?

517
00:28:14,059 --> 00:28:15,059
Go ahead and ask.

518
00:28:15,526 --> 00:28:16,660
Do you remember,

519
00:28:17,496 --> 00:28:19,563
the medicine you sent
to Mi Young three years ago?

520
00:28:19,965 --> 00:28:23,434
The one we sent to our business partners
as holiday gifts from our company?

521
00:28:24,203 --> 00:28:25,436
You mean that one?

522
00:28:25,938 --> 00:28:27,005
Yes.

523
00:28:27,440 --> 00:28:30,140
The health supplement
sent under your name.

524
00:28:30,510 --> 00:28:32,476
- Yes, I remember.
- Was that a coincidence?

525
00:28:33,145 --> 00:28:33,978
Sorry?

526
00:28:34,147 --> 00:28:37,248
The timing was Right when you found out
that your son wasn't yours,

527
00:28:37,750 --> 00:28:40,151
and right when you bumped
into Mi Young, who was pregnant,

528
00:28:40,152 --> 00:28:41,652
you sent that to her.

529
00:28:42,120 --> 00:28:43,321
Was it just a coincidence?

530
00:28:44,223 --> 00:28:46,224
What are you talking about?

531
00:28:46,225 --> 00:28:48,159
Our baby died because of that medicine.

532
00:28:48,762 --> 00:28:50,195
What do you mean, the baby died?

533
00:28:50,196 --> 00:28:51,896
At least, that's what Mi Young believes.

534
00:28:52,363 --> 00:28:54,198
She believes
she miscarried after taking it.

535
00:28:54,533 --> 00:28:56,601
And ever since then,
she's suspected and resented me,

536
00:28:56,602 --> 00:28:58,136
for giving her that medicine.

537
00:28:58,369 --> 00:28:59,470
That's impossible.

538
00:29:00,838 --> 00:29:03,474
That medicine was just
an ordinary supplement that...

539
00:29:03,475 --> 00:29:05,709
The medicine itself
may have been ordinary.

540
00:29:06,578 --> 00:29:08,612
Unless someone tampered with it.

541
00:29:10,383 --> 00:29:11,382
Tampered?

542
00:29:11,617 --> 00:29:13,785
Yes, tampered.

543
00:29:14,185 --> 00:29:15,786
So you're saying...

544
00:29:16,522 --> 00:29:19,567
I deliberately tampered with the medicine,

545
00:29:20,101 --> 00:29:21,860
to harm Mi Young and her baby?

546
00:29:22,861 --> 00:29:24,195
Is that what you mean?

547
00:29:24,196 --> 00:29:27,264
I can't find any other way
to explain what happened.

548
00:29:30,836 --> 00:29:31,769
Does that...

549
00:29:32,404 --> 00:29:34,138
make you feel better?

550
00:29:35,040 --> 00:29:37,643
- What?
- If it turns out that she miscarried,

551
00:29:37,644 --> 00:29:39,175
because she took
the medicine I gave her...

552
00:29:39,645 --> 00:29:42,680
If it turns out that I'm entirely to blame
for her suffering a wound,

553
00:29:42,681 --> 00:29:43,914
she'll never be able to heal from...

554
00:29:44,350 --> 00:29:47,618
Would that make things easier for you?

555
00:29:47,619 --> 00:29:50,555
Cut the bullshit and answer the question.

556
00:29:50,556 --> 00:29:51,522
Please leave.

557
00:29:52,390 --> 00:29:54,290
There's no point
wasting any more time talking.

558
00:29:56,762 --> 00:29:58,296
You tampered with it, didn't you?

559
00:30:02,234 --> 00:30:04,268
You wanted her to have no child,

560
00:30:04,269 --> 00:30:06,638
so it would be easier for you
to divorce and get her back.

561
00:30:07,072 --> 00:30:09,375
That's why you tampered
with that medicine.

562
00:30:09,509 --> 00:30:10,441
Didn't you?

563
00:30:12,478 --> 00:30:13,511
Hey.

564
00:30:14,113 --> 00:30:15,179
Let go.

565
00:30:15,515 --> 00:30:16,614
Do you know why...

566
00:30:17,183 --> 00:30:20,051
I stood by and let her
marry a bastard like you?

567
00:30:20,752 --> 00:30:22,786
Because she chose you.

568
00:30:23,288 --> 00:30:25,923
Because you were the man she wanted.

569
00:30:26,792 --> 00:30:27,859
Listen carefully.

570
00:30:28,660 --> 00:30:31,762
I would die for Mi Young.

571
00:30:32,131 --> 00:30:34,732
I'm nothing like a bastard like you,

572
00:30:34,967 --> 00:30:36,634
who shamelessly cheats on Mi Young.

573
00:30:51,483 --> 00:30:54,085
That hurts.

574
00:30:55,387 --> 00:30:56,953
He could've just talked.

575
00:30:56,954 --> 00:30:58,656
What is he, some kind of gangster?

576
00:30:59,291 --> 00:31:00,825
And he's freaking strong.

577
00:31:03,262 --> 00:31:04,495
Are you okay?

578
00:31:08,297 --> 00:31:10,169
What are you still doing here?

579
00:31:15,140 --> 00:31:17,608
Didn't you say Calvin fired you?

580
00:31:18,310 --> 00:31:19,209
He did.

581
00:31:19,678 --> 00:31:21,879
That's why you rescued me.

582
00:31:22,247 --> 00:31:23,914
So why are you here again?

583
00:31:23,915 --> 00:31:24,982
What do you want?

584
00:31:25,417 --> 00:31:27,118
I'm here to investigate the incident.

585
00:31:27,119 --> 00:31:30,321
Calvin is the prime suspect
for trying to kill me.

586
00:31:30,989 --> 00:31:31,855
What?

587
00:31:32,290 --> 00:31:34,491
The incident where someone
pushed me off the cliff...

588
00:31:34,860 --> 00:31:35,954
It was...

589
00:31:36,768 --> 00:31:38,029
Calvin.

590
00:31:39,601 --> 00:31:40,899
No way.

591
00:31:40,900 --> 00:31:42,266
It's true.

592
00:31:42,600 --> 00:31:44,401
You saw him just now.

593
00:31:44,703 --> 00:31:47,104
He grabbed you by the collar
after only a few words.

594
00:31:47,739 --> 00:31:49,673
Throwing someone off a cliff would be...

595
00:31:50,008 --> 00:31:51,375
nothing to a guy like him.

596
00:31:51,576 --> 00:31:52,576
Fair point.

597
00:31:52,911 --> 00:31:54,945
That guy has a serious
anger-management problem.

598
00:31:54,946 --> 00:31:57,214
I seriously thought I was
going to suffocate to death.

599
00:31:57,615 --> 00:32:00,484
And I'm sure he tampered
with the medicine too.

600
00:32:01,053 --> 00:32:01,986
What?

601
00:32:02,187 --> 00:32:04,388
Were you listening to all of that outside?

602
00:32:04,655 --> 00:32:06,323
I wasn't exactly trying to listen.

603
00:32:06,791 --> 00:32:08,859
What was I supposed to do
when I could hear?

604
00:32:10,595 --> 00:32:12,797
But seeing how furious he got just now,

605
00:32:13,332 --> 00:32:14,732
maybe he really isn't the one.

606
00:32:15,133 --> 00:32:16,867
I'm so confused.

607
00:32:17,035 --> 00:32:18,301
No, it's clear.

608
00:32:18,972 --> 00:32:21,606
Calvin is definitely the culprit.

609
00:32:23,875 --> 00:32:27,010
When you're this stressed,
you should eat something.

610
00:32:27,779 --> 00:32:29,146
Let's get something good to eat.

611
00:32:30,415 --> 00:32:32,649
- No.
- Why?

612
00:32:32,918 --> 00:32:35,720
Not until I clear my name.

613
00:32:36,021 --> 00:32:36,920
Clear your name?

614
00:32:36,921 --> 00:32:39,457
My wife thinks I'm a murderer right now.

615
00:32:39,725 --> 00:32:41,491
Until I find the person responsible for...

616
00:32:41,515 --> 00:32:43,026
the miscarriage and clear my name,

617
00:32:43,596 --> 00:32:44,795
let's not see each other.

618
00:32:44,796 --> 00:32:46,197
What?

619
00:32:46,665 --> 00:32:48,165
What does you being innocent...

620
00:32:48,401 --> 00:32:50,534
have to do with whether we see each other?

621
00:32:50,535 --> 00:32:52,213
Of course it has something to do with it.

622
00:32:52,237 --> 00:32:53,537
This is all because of you.

623
00:32:53,906 --> 00:32:57,377
My wife lost it, and this whole mess
happened because of you.

624
00:32:57,378 --> 00:32:58,676
What are you talking about?

625
00:32:58,777 --> 00:33:00,611
Anyway, I'm leaving.

626
00:33:03,081 --> 00:33:04,448
Wait for me.

627
00:33:11,690 --> 00:33:13,124
Mr. Ji.

628
00:33:14,359 --> 00:33:16,761
Seriously?

629
00:33:31,443 --> 00:33:33,276
It looks even more
dazzling under the lights.

630
00:33:33,578 --> 00:33:35,279
Think about little things like that too.

631
00:33:39,751 --> 00:33:41,785
You have hands and feet and everything.

632
00:33:42,487 --> 00:33:45,489
When did you grow up this much?

633
00:33:46,858 --> 00:33:48,358
Hang in there just a little longer.

634
00:33:49,026 --> 00:33:52,262
Once you come out,
Mommy will take even better care of you.

635
00:33:55,867 --> 00:33:58,068
- Mrs. Baek.
- Yes, come in.

636
00:34:00,972 --> 00:34:03,140
I'm not interrupting anything, am I?

637
00:34:03,842 --> 00:34:04,775
No, you're not.

638
00:34:05,444 --> 00:34:06,978
What is it?

639
00:34:07,579 --> 00:34:08,913
Well.

640
00:34:14,586 --> 00:34:16,754
What's this?

641
00:34:25,330 --> 00:34:26,330
Goodbye.

642
00:34:28,767 --> 00:34:29,700
Mrs. Baek.

643
00:34:30,903 --> 00:34:32,169
This is amazing.

644
00:34:32,504 --> 00:34:35,706
Every customer who came in today
loved the dresses so much,

645
00:34:35,941 --> 00:34:37,074
that they signed right away.

646
00:34:37,742 --> 00:34:41,645
Even the customer who shopped
around several shops in Cheongdam...

647
00:34:41,714 --> 00:34:43,614
booked with us the moment she walked in.

648
00:34:44,015 --> 00:34:45,849
Really? That's great.

649
00:34:46,218 --> 00:34:49,153
It really makes me realize
how amazing Mr. Ji is.

650
00:34:49,520 --> 00:34:52,256
He doesn't even seem
to do that much on the surface.

651
00:34:52,891 --> 00:34:55,960
But how does he manage to create
such perfect dresses every season?

652
00:34:56,661 --> 00:34:57,661
Don't you think?

653
00:34:58,630 --> 00:34:59,496
Right.

654
00:35:02,534 --> 00:35:04,068
Mr. Kang.

655
00:35:05,337 --> 00:35:09,040
There's something I want to ask you.

656
00:35:10,141 --> 00:35:11,041
What is it?

657
00:35:12,677 --> 00:35:13,710
Well.

658
00:35:16,081 --> 00:35:17,214
Excuse me.

659
00:35:19,851 --> 00:35:20,751
Hello.

660
00:35:23,255 --> 00:35:24,422
Welcome.

661
00:35:37,535 --> 00:35:41,171
Won Ho came to see me today.

662
00:35:41,808 --> 00:35:42,773
Did he?

663
00:35:44,109 --> 00:35:46,243
Why? What did he want?

664
00:35:46,745 --> 00:35:48,044
He asked about the medicine...

665
00:35:48,747 --> 00:35:51,214
I sent to your company
about three years ago.

666
00:35:52,050 --> 00:35:52,916
The medicine?

667
00:35:52,917 --> 00:35:56,420
The one I sent under the name
of Calvin Hotel three years ago.

668
00:35:57,122 --> 00:35:58,022
Don't you remember?

669
00:35:58,958 --> 00:36:01,258
The health supplement
in the purple container.

670
00:36:01,727 --> 00:36:02,594
Is it...

671
00:36:03,267 --> 00:36:06,230
similar to the supplements
you gave me last time?

672
00:36:06,565 --> 00:36:07,398
Yes, right.

673
00:36:09,367 --> 00:36:10,533
Take these when you're tired.

674
00:36:11,503 --> 00:36:12,470
Thanks.

675
00:36:19,811 --> 00:36:21,178
(Energy Care Up)

676
00:36:21,613 --> 00:36:24,248
Could it possibly be because of that...

677
00:36:24,950 --> 00:36:26,183
No way.

678
00:36:28,720 --> 00:36:30,888
I never even opened that medicine.

679
00:36:32,524 --> 00:36:33,524
Of course,

680
00:36:35,193 --> 00:36:36,293
I never took it either.

681
00:36:36,861 --> 00:36:38,461
(Energy Care Up)

682
00:36:40,199 --> 00:36:41,098
Really?

683
00:36:41,366 --> 00:36:42,700
That supplement was...

684
00:36:43,501 --> 00:36:46,103
made by a company affiliated with you.

685
00:36:47,172 --> 00:36:50,340
Back then, I couldn't stand
anything that reminded me of you.

686
00:36:52,611 --> 00:36:53,578
Sorry.

687
00:37:01,419 --> 00:37:02,652
What's wrong with you?

688
00:37:03,588 --> 00:37:04,621
Sorry, Mi Young.

689
00:37:06,325 --> 00:37:07,625
I'm really sorry.

690
00:37:09,260 --> 00:37:10,927
When I found out you were pregnant,

691
00:37:12,097 --> 00:37:14,365
I didn't want you
to have a healthy delivery.

692
00:37:16,368 --> 00:37:17,301
That child...

693
00:37:18,804 --> 00:37:20,371
could have been mine.

694
00:37:23,007 --> 00:37:24,341
Honestly, I was angry.

695
00:37:26,712 --> 00:37:27,745
I guess,

696
00:37:29,548 --> 00:37:31,047
I wanted you to suffer the way I had.

697
00:37:34,890 --> 00:37:37,621
Things might have happened to that child,

698
00:37:39,591 --> 00:37:41,358
because I had bad intentions toward you.

699
00:37:43,528 --> 00:37:44,661
Don't do this.

700
00:37:46,564 --> 00:37:47,998
It wasn't your fault.

701
00:37:58,143 --> 00:37:59,743
How could you even think that?

702
00:38:00,445 --> 00:38:02,512
What now?

703
00:38:02,513 --> 00:38:04,181
You went to Calvin, didn't you?

704
00:38:05,017 --> 00:38:06,984
Is Calvin some kind of criminal?

705
00:38:07,819 --> 00:38:10,053
How can you imagine
something so ridiculous?

706
00:38:10,188 --> 00:38:11,855
You called me a murderer,

707
00:38:11,856 --> 00:38:13,790
but Calvin can't even be a criminal?

708
00:38:14,359 --> 00:38:16,660
I had no idea Calvin was such a saint.

709
00:38:17,796 --> 00:38:18,696
Anyway,

710
00:38:19,164 --> 00:38:21,097
you've got the completely wrong person.

711
00:38:21,833 --> 00:38:24,835
The medicine I took had
absolutely nothing to do with him.

712
00:38:25,871 --> 00:38:27,471
Then what was it?

713
00:38:27,472 --> 00:38:30,540
Stop making this so frustrating
and just tell me what happened.

714
00:38:30,876 --> 00:38:33,510
What medicine did you take,
and how did you take it?

715
00:38:33,511 --> 00:38:34,411
That's...

716
00:38:37,081 --> 00:38:38,882
Ask your friend yourself.

717
00:38:38,984 --> 00:38:39,983
My friend?

718
00:38:41,086 --> 00:38:44,055
I seriously have no idea
what you're talking about.

719
00:38:48,494 --> 00:38:50,361
Then let me ask you just one more thing.

720
00:38:51,395 --> 00:38:53,730
Do you still really think I'm a murderer?

721
00:38:53,731 --> 00:38:54,731
That I killed our baby?

722
00:38:55,634 --> 00:38:56,467
Yes.

723
00:38:59,571 --> 00:39:00,571
Then I have no choice,

724
00:39:01,006 --> 00:39:02,105
but to leave again.

725
00:39:03,174 --> 00:39:04,473
Are you leaving the house again?

726
00:39:05,844 --> 00:39:08,479
Could you live under the same roof
with someone you believe is a murderer?

727
00:39:08,647 --> 00:39:11,148
You're really enjoying
I call you a murderer, aren't you?

728
00:39:11,716 --> 00:39:12,649
What?

729
00:39:12,817 --> 00:39:13,884
Am I wrong?

730
00:39:14,119 --> 00:39:15,319
You're just using that...

731
00:39:15,854 --> 00:39:18,022
as an excuse to leave
so you can be with Hee Ju.

732
00:39:18,356 --> 00:39:20,055
You've been pretending
to be angry with me,

733
00:39:20,325 --> 00:39:21,993
but wasn't that
your real motive all along?

734
00:39:21,994 --> 00:39:23,060
Fine.

735
00:39:23,361 --> 00:39:26,163
But you'd better think
about how to handle the consequences.

736
00:39:26,931 --> 00:39:28,332
Why should I care?

737
00:39:28,333 --> 00:39:30,968
No, you'll have to.

738
00:39:31,169 --> 00:39:32,937
Because I'm going to completely shatter...

739
00:39:32,938 --> 00:39:34,672
this ridiculous misconception of yours.

740
00:39:51,689 --> 00:39:53,456
What am I supposed to do now?

741
00:39:54,526 --> 00:39:56,660
I came out here after talking big,

742
00:39:56,661 --> 00:39:59,330
but what exactly is she thinking?

743
00:39:59,631 --> 00:40:04,502
So Mi Young really never told you
what medicine she took, right?

744
00:40:05,203 --> 00:40:06,170
Right.

745
00:40:06,839 --> 00:40:08,772
She told me to ask her friend
or something,

746
00:40:08,773 --> 00:40:10,073
and didn't tell me properly.

747
00:40:10,249 --> 00:40:13,016
She kept saying things
like it was a riddle.

748
00:40:13,344 --> 00:40:14,690
Seriously, it's not like I have
a lot of friends.

749
00:40:14,714 --> 00:40:15,745
You're the only one.

750
00:40:16,715 --> 00:40:17,715
That's right.

751
00:40:18,049 --> 00:40:19,816
I'm the only friend you have.

752
00:40:20,251 --> 00:40:23,254
Anyway, it's really a relief that it's not
the medicine Ah Ri gave, but...

753
00:40:24,156 --> 00:40:26,457
I really don't know what I should do now.

754
00:40:27,024 --> 00:40:29,059
I looked into it after our conversation,

755
00:40:29,828 --> 00:40:31,929
and apparently, there are
quite a few things you shouldn't eat...

756
00:40:32,197 --> 00:40:33,430
when you're pregnant.

757
00:40:35,266 --> 00:40:36,466
Maybe...

758
00:40:37,636 --> 00:40:39,569
your wife just wanted
to put the blame on you.

759
00:40:40,272 --> 00:40:41,838
If she said the miscarriage was her fault,

760
00:40:42,941 --> 00:40:44,174
then it would be too much to bear.

761
00:40:46,044 --> 00:40:47,444
You do have a point.

762
00:40:47,812 --> 00:40:50,480
Wouldn't forgetting about this now...

763
00:40:51,631 --> 00:40:53,551
and ending the divorce on good terms...

764
00:40:54,385 --> 00:40:55,618
be better for the both of you?

765
00:40:57,155 --> 00:40:58,522
Since you two are in the same industry,

766
00:40:58,956 --> 00:41:00,891
even after you get divorced,
you'd still run into each other.

767
00:41:00,892 --> 00:41:02,560
I didn't want to go this far either,

768
00:41:02,561 --> 00:41:05,028
but Mi Young keeps on testing me.

769
00:41:05,029 --> 00:41:06,930
She called me a murderer!

770
00:41:06,931 --> 00:41:08,798
How can I keep quiet
while being called things like that?

771
00:41:08,799 --> 00:41:11,434
That's probably because she lost
her temper over Hee Ju.

772
00:41:12,002 --> 00:41:13,938
If you can just end things
with Hee Ju here...

773
00:41:13,939 --> 00:41:15,305
Hee Ju or not!

774
00:41:15,306 --> 00:41:17,307
I'm going to see this through to the end.

775
00:41:17,308 --> 00:41:18,809
I'll get to the bottom of it...

776
00:41:18,810 --> 00:41:21,678
and clearly show Mi Young
that I'm innocent.

777
00:42:06,858 --> 00:42:08,292
It's what the doctor in charge...

778
00:42:08,980 --> 00:42:11,781
told me when I had my miscarriage.

779
00:42:13,265 --> 00:42:15,165
The medicine that my husband gave me...

780
00:42:16,301 --> 00:42:18,101
was fatal to the fetus.

781
00:42:18,102 --> 00:42:20,938
What the hell are you talking about?
What are you on?

782
00:42:34,218 --> 00:42:35,351
Why do you think...

783
00:42:35,887 --> 00:42:38,888
I stood by watching Mi Young get married
to someone like you?

784
00:42:40,024 --> 00:42:41,992
Because Mi Young chose you.

785
00:42:42,526 --> 00:42:45,094
Because the person
Mi Young wanted was you!

786
00:43:19,764 --> 00:43:20,964
Do you really not remember?

787
00:43:21,632 --> 00:43:23,199
Medication or whatnot,

788
00:43:23,200 --> 00:43:26,069
I never gave you anything
that would harm you!

789
00:43:32,744 --> 00:43:33,811
Then I guess I have no choice...

790
00:43:34,178 --> 00:43:35,245
but to leave again.

791
00:43:36,347 --> 00:43:37,648
You're leaving again?

792
00:43:38,622 --> 00:43:41,391
Can you continue to live
in the same house with a murderer?

793
00:44:05,569 --> 00:44:07,336
(Not currently on air)

794
00:44:36,507 --> 00:44:37,674
Man, it's cold.

795
00:44:39,544 --> 00:44:41,712
Why isn't she here yet? It's freezing.

796
00:44:43,314 --> 00:44:44,180
Won Ho!

797
00:44:44,882 --> 00:44:46,249
Come on, man!

798
00:44:46,784 --> 00:44:48,652
Sorry, Won Ho. I'm late, aren't I?

799
00:44:48,653 --> 00:44:51,020
You're the one who asked to meet first!
How can you be late?

800
00:44:51,021 --> 00:44:51,922
I'm sorry.

801
00:44:52,141 --> 00:44:54,441
In exchange,
I promise you'll have fun today.

802
00:44:54,525 --> 00:44:56,059
You better.

803
00:44:56,060 --> 00:44:58,194
- Let's go.
- Where are we going?

804
00:44:58,195 --> 00:44:59,596
There.

805
00:45:00,198 --> 00:45:02,166
(Bowling Alley)

806
00:45:11,909 --> 00:45:13,843
What? Are you tired?

807
00:45:14,278 --> 00:45:15,579
Yes, a little.

808
00:45:15,580 --> 00:45:17,147
You know I'm usually asleep at this hour.

809
00:45:17,148 --> 00:45:19,015
That's the problem with you!

810
00:45:19,384 --> 00:45:21,318
You work like a dog when you're at work...

811
00:45:21,319 --> 00:45:23,320
and sleep like a corpse
when you're resting.

812
00:45:23,422 --> 00:45:25,322
When do you even have fun?

813
00:45:25,323 --> 00:45:27,257
That's why I'm here today.

814
00:45:27,636 --> 00:45:28,558
That's right.

815
00:45:29,476 --> 00:45:31,362
It's been a while, so let's loosen up...

816
00:45:31,446 --> 00:45:33,413
and blow off all that built-up stress.

817
00:45:33,798 --> 00:45:34,665
Okay?

818
00:45:34,966 --> 00:45:35,766
Okay.

819
00:45:38,870 --> 00:45:41,038
They should be here any minute now.

820
00:45:42,140 --> 00:45:43,240
Are you expecting someone else?

821
00:45:44,576 --> 00:45:46,076
Well...

822
00:45:46,778 --> 00:45:47,844
They're here!

823
00:45:48,479 --> 00:45:49,746
Mr. Kang, over here!

824
00:45:52,300 --> 00:45:53,333
Why you little...

825
00:45:53,417 --> 00:45:56,286
- Ah Ri, you...
- Just stay quiet.

826
00:45:59,474 --> 00:46:01,275
- Forget it. I'm leaving.
- Won Ho, come on!

827
00:46:01,359 --> 00:46:02,792
Don't be like that!
Let's hang out with them.

828
00:46:02,793 --> 00:46:05,028
Why the hell are you doing
things I never asked you to do!

829
00:46:05,029 --> 00:46:06,129
Just once. Let's go.

830
00:46:06,130 --> 00:46:07,330
Seriously...

831
00:46:08,833 --> 00:46:09,733
Goodness.

832
00:46:13,938 --> 00:46:15,872
I'm sorry. We're a bit late, aren't we?

833
00:46:15,873 --> 00:46:18,675
No! You're just on time.

834
00:46:19,010 --> 00:46:22,713
Well, I guess we can form teams
and start right away then.

835
00:46:22,714 --> 00:46:24,514
Ah Ri, what are you doing?

836
00:46:24,817 --> 00:46:26,517
Are you serious right now?

837
00:46:26,518 --> 00:46:28,853
I'm sorry. But if I'd told you,

838
00:46:28,854 --> 00:46:30,420
you guys wouldn't have come.

839
00:46:30,421 --> 00:46:32,222
- So why?
- You knew that and still did this?

840
00:46:32,456 --> 00:46:34,624
Can't you two just be cool
and make up already?

841
00:46:35,226 --> 00:46:37,227
Me, as well as everyone at J&amp;WHITE...

842
00:46:37,228 --> 00:46:39,262
are all on edge because of you two.

843
00:46:39,496 --> 00:46:40,997
He's right!

844
00:46:41,298 --> 00:46:42,599
Why don't we just think...

845
00:46:42,767 --> 00:46:45,368
of today as a workshop or something.

846
00:46:45,637 --> 00:46:47,837
We can play some games
and work on our teamwork.

847
00:46:48,272 --> 00:46:49,807
How does that sound, Mr. Ji?

848
00:46:51,309 --> 00:46:53,676
Well, I don't really mind.

849
00:46:54,877 --> 00:46:57,812
Alright then. We'll just consider...

850
00:46:58,517 --> 00:47:01,017
this a workshop or something,
like you said, Ms. Song.

851
00:47:02,186 --> 00:47:04,754
Sounds great! Shall we get started, then?

852
00:47:04,990 --> 00:47:06,957
The losing team pays for drinks!

853
00:47:07,258 --> 00:47:08,225
Okay!

854
00:47:18,402 --> 00:47:19,702
Okay!

855
00:47:31,315 --> 00:47:32,815
Dang it!

856
00:47:49,500 --> 00:47:50,433
Nice!

857
00:48:18,896 --> 00:48:20,397
I told you, stoop down and throw it!
Look at me.

858
00:48:20,398 --> 00:48:22,599
Throw it straight like this.
Don't swing your arm like that.

859
00:48:25,369 --> 00:48:26,269
I did it!

860
00:48:37,982 --> 00:48:38,848
Yes!

861
00:48:43,020 --> 00:48:43,953
It's okay.

862
00:48:46,190 --> 00:48:47,056
Yes!

863
00:48:52,263 --> 00:48:53,330
All right,

864
00:48:53,331 --> 00:48:54,531
this is the last one.

865
00:48:55,833 --> 00:48:58,601
As long as Mi Young doesn't get a strike,

866
00:48:58,602 --> 00:49:00,402
we win.

867
00:49:00,403 --> 00:49:01,304
Okay, let's go.

868
00:49:01,407 --> 00:49:02,672
It won't be easy.

869
00:49:02,673 --> 00:49:03,740
We got this. We've basically won.

870
00:49:03,741 --> 00:49:04,607
Mi Young,

871
00:49:05,409 --> 00:49:06,509
you got this!

872
00:49:17,221 --> 00:49:19,222
Go!

873
00:49:20,358 --> 00:49:21,625
Okay!

874
00:49:27,732 --> 00:49:29,403
- That's right!
- We won!

875
00:49:29,404 --> 00:49:30,834
Bang bang!

876
00:49:32,036 --> 00:49:34,604
Everyone, cheers!

877
00:49:41,746 --> 00:49:43,146
Oh, wow.

878
00:49:44,121 --> 00:49:46,221
Can we get one more? Thank you.

879
00:49:46,517 --> 00:49:49,118
Wow, Ms. Song,
you're really going all out today.

880
00:49:49,553 --> 00:49:51,387
Are you okay?

881
00:49:51,388 --> 00:49:53,723
Of course.

882
00:49:53,724 --> 00:49:55,791
It's me, Song Ah Ri.

883
00:49:55,792 --> 00:49:59,462
This is nothing.

884
00:49:59,631 --> 00:50:01,398
Anyone can tell
you're really drunk, Ms. Song.

885
00:50:01,833 --> 00:50:02,799
You should stop drinking now.

886
00:50:02,800 --> 00:50:06,136
Anyone can tell I'm not drunk,
for your information.

887
00:50:08,806 --> 00:50:10,340
Where am I?

888
00:50:11,108 --> 00:50:12,675
What round is this?

889
00:50:12,676 --> 00:50:13,710
Sorry?

890
00:50:14,278 --> 00:50:16,579
Ms. Song, you should get going now.

891
00:50:17,081 --> 00:50:19,249
I'll help Ms. Song get a taxi.

892
00:50:19,450 --> 00:50:20,661
Are you sure you'll be okay on your own?

893
00:50:21,085 --> 00:50:22,085
Do you want me to go with you?

894
00:50:22,086 --> 00:50:23,219
No, it's okay.

895
00:50:23,454 --> 00:50:25,555
You two should talk until I come back.

896
00:50:25,673 --> 00:50:28,174
- Ms. Song, let's go!
- Are we going another round?

897
00:50:28,258 --> 00:50:29,995
- Come on.
- Nice! Let's go.

898
00:50:29,996 --> 00:50:32,061
- You have to go.
- Next round! Let's go!

899
00:50:32,062 --> 00:50:34,197
- Careful.
- We need to go at least three rounds.

900
00:50:45,910 --> 00:50:47,043
Come back home.

901
00:50:48,959 --> 00:50:49,913
Do you mean it?

902
00:50:49,914 --> 00:50:52,114
You can't keep staying at the motel.

903
00:50:52,417 --> 00:50:54,484
It's not like I kicked you out on purpose
or anything.

904
00:50:55,019 --> 00:50:57,086
Then, are you taking back...

905
00:50:57,721 --> 00:50:58,821
you calling me a murderer?

906
00:50:59,623 --> 00:51:00,423
What?

907
00:51:00,691 --> 00:51:02,959
There must be a reason
you're suddenly doing this.

908
00:51:03,294 --> 00:51:05,462
Did you clear all the misunderstandings
you had about me?

909
00:51:05,571 --> 00:51:08,306
Are you going to stop blaming
the pills now?

910
00:51:08,700 --> 00:51:09,699
Blaming the pills?

911
00:51:13,437 --> 00:51:15,305
If you don't want to come home,
then don't.

912
00:51:15,306 --> 00:51:17,741
Just stay at the motel
and have fun with Hee Ju.

913
00:51:17,742 --> 00:51:19,342
Are you playing with me or something?

914
00:51:19,343 --> 00:51:20,877
Why do you keep changing your mind?

915
00:51:20,878 --> 00:51:23,479
What about you? Why the hell can't you get
it through your thick head?

916
00:51:23,480 --> 00:51:24,813
Thick head?

917
00:51:24,814 --> 00:51:26,315
Did you really just say that?

918
00:51:26,316 --> 00:51:29,285
Yes, I did! What? You going to hit me?
Go ahead! Hit me!

919
00:51:29,286 --> 00:51:31,588
I will!

920
00:51:31,755 --> 00:51:33,556
Do whatever you want!

921
00:51:33,557 --> 00:51:35,091
- It hurts! My head hurts!
- Whatever!

922
00:51:37,595 --> 00:51:39,729
Seriously! What's wrong with you two?

923
00:51:42,867 --> 00:51:44,534
What are you doing, martial arts
or something?

924
00:51:46,437 --> 00:51:47,370
This won't do.

925
00:51:47,905 --> 00:51:49,505
I've got to force you two to smile
or something.

926
00:51:50,307 --> 00:51:51,374
Excuse me!

927
00:51:52,593 --> 00:51:54,994
I'm sorry, but can you take
a picture of us?

928
00:51:55,078 --> 00:51:56,412
Why are you suddenly taking a picture?

929
00:51:56,413 --> 00:51:58,381
Stick together. Ms. Baek! Come closer.

930
00:51:58,382 --> 00:52:00,316
Okay, everyone, look over there and smile.

931
00:52:00,485 --> 00:52:03,253
On three. One, two, three.

932
00:52:11,395 --> 00:52:13,262
Take the taxi home together with Mi Young.

933
00:52:14,498 --> 00:52:15,364
What?

934
00:52:15,900 --> 00:52:18,301
Hurry and go smooth things over with her.

935
00:52:22,740 --> 00:52:25,275
- Hurry up. Go.
- All right.

936
00:52:33,183 --> 00:52:34,049
Hey.

937
00:52:34,985 --> 00:52:36,986
Oh my! Are you okay?

938
00:52:38,289 --> 00:52:40,123
Are you okay? What happened?

939
00:52:40,124 --> 00:52:41,892
My coat got stuck in the door,

940
00:52:41,893 --> 00:52:42,792
so I was trying to get it out.

941
00:52:43,160 --> 00:52:45,493
- Are you okay?
- It's fine! Just go!

942
00:52:45,494 --> 00:52:46,731
You can go.

943
00:52:46,732 --> 00:52:48,097
I'll drop Won Ho off.

944
00:52:48,098 --> 00:52:49,932
I'm sorry.

945
00:52:55,940 --> 00:52:57,774
Won Ho, let me see. Does it hurt a lot?

946
00:52:58,108 --> 00:52:59,442
Of course it hurts!

947
00:53:00,844 --> 00:53:01,778
Does it hurt a lot?

948
00:53:08,485 --> 00:53:09,552
Hello?

949
00:53:09,787 --> 00:53:11,020
Guess you're still sleeping.

950
00:53:12,156 --> 00:53:14,124
What? Why did you call me?

951
00:53:15,159 --> 00:53:16,459
You didn't get evidence, did you?

952
00:53:17,061 --> 00:53:18,462
I will soon.

953
00:53:18,463 --> 00:53:20,129
I have the evidence.

954
00:53:20,698 --> 00:53:21,565
What?

955
00:53:21,566 --> 00:53:24,234
It seemed like you had no ability
or will to actually find evidence,

956
00:53:24,702 --> 00:53:27,370
but were stirring people up
and wearing everyone out.

957
00:53:27,838 --> 00:53:29,505
So I just found it myself.

958
00:53:31,508 --> 00:53:33,776
I'll give you two hours. Come get it.

959
00:53:39,717 --> 00:53:41,051
Dang it. The angle is...

960
00:53:41,317 --> 00:53:42,685
What? Is there a problem?

961
00:53:42,686 --> 00:53:44,253
It does look like they're kissing,

962
00:53:44,622 --> 00:53:46,222
but it doesn't show clearly on the screen.

963
00:53:46,690 --> 00:53:47,857
You're right.

964
00:53:48,672 --> 00:53:51,206
I'll let you know if they come back again.

965
00:53:51,829 --> 00:53:52,695
Thank you.

966
00:53:57,668 --> 00:53:58,534
You've...

967
00:53:59,069 --> 00:54:01,303
helped me so much.
How can I ever repay you?

968
00:54:01,639 --> 00:54:04,174
It's nothing. I like helping.

969
00:54:05,576 --> 00:54:07,877
You like it?

970
00:54:14,918 --> 00:54:16,352
It seems you cut your hair.

971
00:54:16,353 --> 00:54:19,188
You look really good. It's pretty.

972
00:54:19,690 --> 00:54:20,556
Is it?

973
00:54:21,191 --> 00:54:22,124
Yes.

974
00:54:29,633 --> 00:54:33,302
There's something I'd like
your legal advice on.

975
00:54:33,671 --> 00:54:34,638
Sure.

976
00:54:35,372 --> 00:54:37,707
You can ask me anything.

977
00:54:37,708 --> 00:54:40,609
Thank you. How can I get a guest...

978
00:54:40,610 --> 00:54:42,912
to leave their room?

979
00:54:42,913 --> 00:54:44,747
Are you talking about a forced eviction?

980
00:54:44,748 --> 00:54:47,049
Yes, that. A forced eviction.
How do I do that?

981
00:54:47,851 --> 00:54:49,718
If they're a fugitive on the run,

982
00:54:49,719 --> 00:54:51,521
or they've damaged room fixtures...

983
00:54:51,522 --> 00:54:53,055
and caused financial loss.

984
00:54:53,958 --> 00:54:56,659
If we evict this guest
because they've got no decency,

985
00:54:56,760 --> 00:54:59,195
would that count
as a mitigating circumstance?

986
00:54:59,443 --> 00:55:00,676
No decency?

987
00:55:01,665 --> 00:55:03,032
That's a bit of a gray area.

988
00:55:03,667 --> 00:55:04,567
Why?

989
00:55:04,802 --> 00:55:07,237
Do you have a problematic customer
in the building?

990
00:55:07,371 --> 00:55:10,073
Yes. She won't leave
even after we offered her a refund,

991
00:55:10,170 --> 00:55:11,670
and she keeps threatening me and my mom.

992
00:55:11,809 --> 00:55:12,809
Threatening?

993
00:55:13,678 --> 00:55:14,644
It's her!

994
00:55:15,679 --> 00:55:17,613
- Excuse me, ma'am.
- Ms. An!

995
00:55:18,816 --> 00:55:19,682
What?

996
00:55:30,661 --> 00:55:31,628
Lawyer?

997
00:55:32,229 --> 00:55:33,930
My client...

998
00:55:38,279 --> 00:55:39,068
An Hee Ju.

999
00:55:40,623 --> 00:55:43,391
is about to press charges against you,
Ms. An.

1000
00:55:43,607 --> 00:55:44,640
Press charges?

1001
00:55:50,881 --> 00:55:53,216
I heard that you threatened the owner.

1002
00:55:53,751 --> 00:55:54,717
What?

1003
00:55:54,718 --> 00:55:57,086
Why do you insist on staying
at this motel?

1004
00:55:58,756 --> 00:56:00,523
Why are you so set
on this particular motel?

1005
00:56:01,325 --> 00:56:02,225
Excuse me.

1006
00:56:02,427 --> 00:56:04,427
I'm a bit busy right now.

1007
00:56:05,395 --> 00:56:08,163
When we meet again, I'll tell you then.

1008
00:56:08,465 --> 00:56:10,132
You don't seem that busy.

1009
00:56:10,334 --> 00:56:12,635
I'm on my way to catch
a murderer right now.

1010
00:56:13,977 --> 00:56:14,944
A murderer?

1011
00:56:15,071 --> 00:56:16,439
If the murderer gets away,

1012
00:56:17,141 --> 00:56:18,741
are you going to catch that person for me?

1013
00:56:26,850 --> 00:56:27,917
I told you.

1014
00:56:28,185 --> 00:56:31,254
Her attitude is downright nasty.

1015
00:56:31,962 --> 00:56:33,094
It's what?

1016
00:56:33,524 --> 00:56:35,525
downright nasty.

1017
00:56:36,794 --> 00:56:40,296
You're right.
Her attitude is downright nasty.

1018
00:56:46,069 --> 00:56:47,036
Here.

1019
00:56:47,337 --> 00:56:50,039
Icing it could make it better faster.

1020
00:56:51,708 --> 00:56:54,476
It's really a relief
that there wasn't any bleeding.

1021
00:56:54,979 --> 00:56:56,879
Are you worrying about me now?

1022
00:56:57,881 --> 00:56:59,014
I'm leaving.

1023
00:56:59,383 --> 00:57:01,184
Can't you just tell me?

1024
00:57:09,960 --> 00:57:12,228
The medication that you took
three years ago.

1025
00:57:13,500 --> 00:57:16,132
Can you just tell me directly
instead of going around in circles?

1026
00:57:17,384 --> 00:57:19,585
What medication you took,

1027
00:57:19,669 --> 00:57:21,771
and why you keep mistaking me
for a murderer.

1028
00:57:21,772 --> 00:57:24,306
I want to hear your story first
before I make any decision.

1029
00:57:25,342 --> 00:57:26,208
Decision?

1030
00:57:26,577 --> 00:57:28,611
Whether I keep denying it,

1031
00:57:31,448 --> 00:57:32,615
or kneel before you...

1032
00:57:32,616 --> 00:57:34,617
and beg with all my heart for forgiveness.

1033
00:57:34,785 --> 00:57:36,152
Beg for forgiveness? You?

1034
00:57:36,186 --> 00:57:37,419
If it's really my fault,

1035
00:57:37,503 --> 00:57:40,038
I'll accept it without hesitation
and beg for forgiveness.

1036
00:57:43,627 --> 00:57:44,627
So tell me.

1037
00:57:45,829 --> 00:57:46,896
Three years ago,

1038
00:57:48,031 --> 00:57:49,465
what was that medication you took?

1039
00:57:55,606 --> 00:57:56,506
It can't be.

1040
00:57:57,108 --> 00:57:58,174
Why is this person...

1041
00:57:58,575 --> 00:57:59,442
Are you disappointed?

1042
00:58:00,177 --> 00:58:02,011
Because the person who pushed you
off the cliff...

1043
00:58:02,412 --> 00:58:03,379
isn't me?

1044
00:58:04,014 --> 00:58:04,847
Is this...

1045
00:58:06,250 --> 00:58:07,217
real?

1046
00:58:07,852 --> 00:58:09,185
It's not fabricated?

1047
00:58:09,353 --> 00:58:11,087
If you're curious,
go check it out yourself.

1048
00:58:11,839 --> 00:58:13,973
Around the time you fell off the cliff,

1049
00:58:14,057 --> 00:58:15,591
within 30 minutes before and after,

1050
00:58:15,893 --> 00:58:17,760
the person who came down
to the parking lot below the cliff,

1051
00:58:18,529 --> 00:58:20,629
apart from the couple
whose photos you were shooting,

1052
00:58:20,630 --> 00:58:21,797
was that person alone.

1053
00:58:23,583 --> 00:58:24,433
That person.

1054
00:58:28,405 --> 00:58:30,272
This is the most I can do for you.

1055
00:58:31,374 --> 00:58:33,308
Whether you get revenge or make them pay,

1056
00:58:33,803 --> 00:58:35,036
the rest is up to you.

1057
00:58:35,491 --> 00:58:36,745
That's none of my business.

1058
00:58:39,535 --> 00:58:42,337
I just don't understand
why I have to explain this to you.

1059
00:58:42,486 --> 00:58:44,420
I really don't get it.

1060
00:58:45,255 --> 00:58:46,689
All right, I'm sorry too.

1061
00:58:47,190 --> 00:58:48,957
Even though you resent me this much,

1062
00:58:49,712 --> 00:58:52,715
I still can't make sense of any of it,
and for that, I'm sorry too.

1063
00:58:53,597 --> 00:58:54,830
So please, Mi Young,

1064
00:58:55,499 --> 00:58:57,400
just let it all out now.

1065
00:58:58,027 --> 00:59:00,629
About the drug
that put you through all this,

1066
00:59:00,910 --> 00:59:03,579
I need to hear it from you directly.

1067
00:59:12,249 --> 00:59:14,083
The thing that put Dal Rae in danger...

1068
00:59:15,319 --> 00:59:16,486
was the herbal medicine.

1069
00:59:17,321 --> 00:59:18,821
Not the medication Calvin gave me.

1070
00:59:19,523 --> 00:59:20,356
Herbal medicine?

1071
00:59:26,363 --> 00:59:27,530
Do you seriously not remember?

1072
00:59:29,033 --> 00:59:31,634
The one Kyung Tae brought me
because you asked him to.

1073
00:59:33,770 --> 00:59:34,738
Kyung Tae?

1074
01:00:31,394 --> 01:00:34,396
(OK! Let's Get Divorced)

1075
01:00:34,782 --> 01:00:36,516
It's been three years.
What's the point now?

1076
01:00:36,600 --> 01:00:38,901
Even now, you should repent and apologize.

1077
01:00:39,302 --> 01:00:40,569
And what would that change?

1078
01:00:40,570 --> 01:00:42,104
That was today.

1079
01:00:43,507 --> 01:00:44,574
Time sure goes fast.

1080
01:00:45,010 --> 01:00:46,909
Do you know what really hurts?

1081
01:00:47,677 --> 01:00:48,543
That my husband...

1082
01:00:49,046 --> 01:00:50,513
already forgot everything.

1083
01:00:51,665 --> 01:00:53,966
The brooch that Mi Young lost.

1084
01:00:54,043 --> 01:00:56,144
I want to hear some more about this.

1085
01:00:56,553 --> 01:00:58,387
You said you'd make Mi Young happy.

1086
01:00:58,822 --> 01:01:01,023
How do you know
whether she cries or laughs every day?

1087
01:01:01,258 --> 01:01:02,224
She cried yesterday too.

1088
01:01:03,093 --> 01:01:04,093
Because of you.

1089
01:01:09,720 --> 01:01:11,740
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
